# Rust proxy service
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# packages/proxy/Cargo.lock IS tracked, and must be.
#
# This used to be ignored, with the reasoning that Cargo never reads a member
# lockfile — true for a build run from the repo, and false for the one that
# ships. The proxy image is built with `packages/proxy` as its Docker context,
# so inside the image there is no workspace root and the Dockerfile's
# `COPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock ./` needs a lockfile right here. Ignoring it meant
# a clean checkout could not build the proxy at all — the build fails with
# `"/Cargo.lock": not found`.
#
# The enterprise tree fixed this and the fix landed in one repo. That left the
# defect in the open-core repo — the one anyone can actually clone. `.gitignore`
# is a root file and the parity gate compares directories, so nothing could
# have caught it.
# Standalone bench fixture crate — not a workspace member, never tracked.
packages/proxy/benches/wasm_guest/Cargo.lock

# Prebuilt proxy binary — the CLI downloads per-platform assets from GitHub
# Releases (see tools/cli/src/commands/connect.ts), so committing a 39.7MB
# single-platform binary here only taxes every clone.
packages/proxy/bin/intutic-proxy

